# CI Milestones

When the user asks to start new work, open an issue, commit, open a PR, or push, run the matching CI skill (each reviews before the git action and respects consent):

| Intent | Skill |
|---|---|
| Start new work / new branch | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/worktree/SKILL.md` |
| Open / create a GitHub issue | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/issue/SKILL.md` |
| Commit | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/commit/SKILL.md` |
| Open / create a PR | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/pr/SKILL.md` |
| Push | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/push/SKILL.md` |
| Fix-until-clean self-review | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/local-review-loop/SKILL.md` |
| Autonomous PR review-fix loop | `.cursor/skills/code/ci/pr-review-loop/SKILL.md` |

See `.cursor/rules/behaviors/code-review-gate.mdc` for the gate, `behaviors/worktree-first.mdc` for worktree defaults, and `behaviors/git-*-consent.mdc` for consent rules.
